Q. What is On-Demand instance?
Ans : 
An On-Demand instance is a type of Amazon EC2 instance pricing model where:
1. You pay by the hour or second (depending on the instance type).
2. There is no long-term commitment.
3. You can launch, stop, and terminate instances at any time.
4. You're only charged for the time the instance is running.

Q. What is Reserved Instance?
Ans : 
It is an AWS pricing option where you commit to using EC2 for 1 or 3 years to get a discount compared to On-Demand pricing.
You get upto 75% siscount.

Q. What is Spot Instance?
Ans : 
It is a cheap EC2 instance provided by AWS using its unused server capacity. AWS can take it back at any time.

Q. What is dedicated host?
Ans :
1. A physical server reserved for you.
2. You can see and control the host.
3. Place EC2 instances yourself.
4. BYOL licenses (Oracle, SQL Server, SAP)
5. Compliance & auditing	
